# OpenSSL wrapper for the cpp_network workspace.
#
# OpenSSL's upstream source is a configure/make project without a native Bazel
# build. Per the 001 proposal (docs/architecture/host-openssl-build.md), the
# host TLS backend is OpenSSL linked into libcurl. Building OpenSSL from source
# in Bazel requires a configure step (generated headers/asm), which is deferred
# to the protocol implementation phase.
#
# This package documents the dependency contract and provides a stub target so
# the engineering skeleton stays buildable. The real `openssl` cc_library will
# be introduced with the TLS implementation (src/tls).
package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

# NOTE: `openssl` target intentionally omitted until the TLS implementation
# phase defines how OpenSSL is built (foreign_cc / prebuilt / system lib).
